00:43:49,180 --> 00:43:50,480
substrates there is.

786
00:43:50,580 --> 00:43:52,160
No two people are the same.

787
00:43:52,260 --> 00:43:56,500
Your inherent ethnicity, your diet, your food,

788
00:43:56,600 --> 00:44:02,760
all changes on an ongoing basis the composition of your skin

789
00:44:02,860 --> 00:44:04,260
and what's on the surface.

790
00:44:04,360 --> 00:44:05,400
And what does this mean?

791
00:44:05,401 --> 00:44:06,300
And what does this mean?

792
00:44:06,301 --> 00:44:09,500
This means you have an ever-changing substrate

793
00:44:09,501 --> 00:44:11,940
that you're trying to stick to.

794
00:44:11,941 --> 00:44:14,200
But the adhesive does more than stick.

795
00:44:14,201 --> 00:44:16,740
It's also involved in the drug's delivery.

796
00:44:16,741 --> 00:44:19,080
You have a controlled release that

797
00:44:19,081 --> 00:44:23,760
is directly related to the ability of the active ingredient

798
00:44:23,761 --> 00:44:29,920
to work its way through the adhesive mass into the skin.

799
00:44:29,921 --> 00:44:33,520
From human skin to the skin of an airplane,

800
00:44:33,521 --> 00:44:36,020
From the minute applications in computers

801
00:44:36,021 --> 00:44:39,400
to the maximal amounts of adhesive pumped into hulls.

802
00:44:39,401 --> 00:44:43,400
From speed boats to subflooring, without fanfare,

